    "narrative": "With the Austin Waves roster currently restricted by a slate of team off-days for core anchors like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, we are operating with a skeleton crew for today\u2019s matchups. **Liam Hicks** earns the nod as our strongest play with a 52.87 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Armstrong (xERA 4.35) is bolstered by a potent dynamic platoon advantage and a solidified spot in the #5 hole, providing him the best runway for counting stats. **Brayan Rocchio** rounds out the active lineup with a 47.20 score; while his production is suppressed by an unfavorable #9 batting position, he remains a marginal start due to a high-utility matchup against Martinez, N.\n\nOur bench decisions were largely dictated by the limited volume of active games today, but **Luis Robert Jr.** remains the primary concern, sitting firmly on the IL. We are actively monitoring the status of bench options like **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** to ensure we are ready to cycle them back into the active rotation once their respective clubs return to action. Given the scarcity of stolen bases in our 5x5 Roto framework, we are exercising extreme caution with players like **Nasim Nunez** and **Wade Meckler**; their profiles are essential to our late-game agility, but they remain benched today to preserve our remaining game caps for higher-leverage situations. With **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Franklin Arias** also unavailable due to the schedule, today is strictly about efficiency over volume.",
